    <string name="cloud_sync_section">Synchronisation</string>
    <string name="cloud_sync_switch">Synchronise my vaults through this service</string>
    <string name="cloud_sync_explain">The cloud keeps one encrypted copy of each vault. KeyNexa downloads it, merges it with your local vault and uploads the result only when nothing else changed it, so two devices that are never on at the same time end up the same. The file is encrypted exactly like the copies: the service only sees the encrypted file. Older versions of an entry stay in its history, and deleting the vault on one device deletes it everywhere after the next synchronisation.</string>
